'''Pope Stephen VIII''' (IX), was a native of [[Germany]], was [[pope]] from about [[July 14]], [[939]] until his death towards the end of [[October]], [[942]].  

During his pontificate he was subject to [[Alberic]], Prince of the Romans, and did not effectively rule the Papal States. His period as pope was during a brief interruption from the period when the church had been ruled by the so-called &quot;[[pornocracy]]&quot; of Theodora and [[Marozia]], [[Rome|Roman]] noblewomen.

There is a problem numbering the popes Stephen — see [[Stephen (ephemeral pope)]] for the explanation.

