      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Panda''' can have several different meanings:
* The '''[[Giant Panda]]''' is a large black-and-white [[mammal]] in the [[bear]] family.
* The '''[[Red Panda]]''' is a [[mammal]] which may be related to the [[raccoon]] or [[bear]].
* The genus ''[[Panda (plant)|Panda]]'', of the family [[Euphorbiaceae]].
* The '''[[Fiat Panda]]''' and the [[Fiat Panda (2003)|Panda Nuova]] are models of car manufactured by [[Fiat]].
* '''[[Panda Software]]''' is a software company specialising in [[antivirus]] [[software]] [http://www.pandasoftware.com]
* A '''[[panda car]]''' is a patrol car used by the [[British police]].
* '''[[Panda Express]]''' is a fast-food [[China|Chinese]] restaurant chain operating in the [[USA]].
*In [[medicine]], '''PANDAS''' stands for [[P.A.N.D.A.S.|Pediatric Autoimmune Neuropsychiatric Disorders Associated with Streptoccal infections]] [http://intramural.nimh.nih.gov/pdn/web.htm], a hypothesized form of [[pediatric]] [[neuropsychiatric]] [[disease|disorder]] typically manifesting symptoms similar to [[Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder]] 
* In a naval context '''PANDA''' can refer to [[Predictive Analysis for Naval Deployment Activities]].
*'''[[Panda_(musician)|Panda]]''' is a [[Netherlands|Dutch]] [[electronic music|electronic musician]].
*'''[[Panda (mexican group)|Panda]]''' is another [[Rock in Spanish|Mexican]] [[punk rock|Punk]] group.
*[[P.A.N.D.A.S.]] (Pediatric Autoimmune Neuropsychiatric Disorders Associated with Streptococcal infections) is a class of diseases.
*'''[[Wegener Panda]]''' is a noise reduction system used on audio subcarriers on [[analogue television|analogue]] [[satellite television]] in Europe.

{{disambig}}

