  <page>
    <title>Pacifist organisation</title>
    <id>24374</id>
    <revision>
      <id>23830870</id>
      <timestamp>2005-09-23T13:46:54Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Logophile</username>
        <id>163429</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">A '''Pacifist organisation''' promotes the [[pacifism|pacifist]] principles of standing against war and [[aggression]].  Some organisations are concerned only with the removal of [[nuclear weapon]]s from war although they may call for suspension of hostilities as well.  Amongst other organisations are those which deal with other concerns but which have a strong pacific element.

Pacifist organisations :
* [[Religious Society of Friends]] (Quakers)
* [[Mennonites]]
* [[Christian Peacemaker Teams]]
* [[Christian anarchism]]
* [[Fellowship of Reconciliation]]

Nuclear pacifist organisations :
* [[Pugwash Conferences on Science and World Affairs|Pugwash]]
* [[CND]]

Organisations which cite pacifism as an aim :
* [[Greenpeace]] 

==External links==
* [http://www.nonviolence.org Nonviolence.org]
* [http://www.anglicanpeacemaker.org.uk Anglican Pacifist Fellowship]
{{Poli-stub}}

[[Category:Pacifism]]</text>
    </revision>
