      <minor />
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Phalanx''' ([[Greek language|Greek]] word from ''phalangos'', meaning ''[[Finger]]'') can refer to:

* '''[[phalanx formation]]''' in ancient warfare.
* In anatomy, '''[[phalanx bones]]''' refer to a row of finger or toe bones.
* '''[[Phalanx CIWS]]''' is a naval defense system.
* '''[[Phalanx (comics)|The Phalanx]]''' are a [[fictional species]] of villainous mechanical [[Extraterrestrial life|alien]]s in [[Marvel Comics]]' [[X-Men]] [[comic book]]s.
* Phalanx '''[http://www2.etown.edu/Phalanx]''' is the premier all-male a capella group at Elizabethtown College.
* '''[[Phalanx (video game)|Phalanx]]''' is also a [[space-shooter]] [[Computer and video games|video game]].
*[[The Phalanx]] was a [[Fourierist]] journal published in [[New York City]] from [[1843]] to [[1845]]
* [[North American Phalanx]], a utopian community organized on proto-communist Fourierist principles.
*[[Phalanstère]] is the name [[Charles Fourier]] gave to a specific building layout in accordance with [[Fourierist]] principles.
*[[Phalanx art school]] was a private art school around 1900 located in [[Munich]]
* Phalanx VTOL (Vertical Takeoff and Landing) Airplane, circa late 1980s, no other information.

See also

*[[Falange]]

{{disambig}}

