  <page>
    <title>Philemon</title>
    <id>24442</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41582064</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-28T07:47:09Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Earbox</username>
        <id>575934</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Philemon''' may refer to:

* [[Philemon of Colossae]], the recipient of Paul's [[Epistle to Philemon]].
* The husband of Baucis in Greek mythology. See [[Baucis and Philemon]].
* [[Philemon (poet)|Philemon]], a poet of the [[Athenian Democracy]].
* ''[[Philemon Martyr]]'', a play by [[Jacob Bidermann]].
* ''Philemon'', a musical by [[Tom Jones (writer)|Tom Jones]] and [[Harvey Schmidt]].
* Philemon, [[Carl Jung]]'s wise spirit guide.
* ''[[Philemon (genus)|Philemon]]'', a genus of birds in the family [[Meliphagidae]].

{{disambig}}

[[de:Philemon]]
[[fr:Philémon (écrivain)]]
[[ja:フィレモン]]
[[pl:Filemon]]
[[sv:Filemon]]</text>
